I was helping the facilities crew pick paint swatches for every conference room in the building. The rule is simple: every room gets exactly one swatch, and if two rooms share a doorway they can’t be finished in the same swatch. The better plans are the ones that use fewer different swatches overall — you judge that by counting how many distinct swatches end up being used. Nothing can be skipped or double-covered: every room needs a single swatch and no pair of adjacent rooms may match. The concrete room-and-door layout is shown below.

